## Inspection
Extracted frames at t = 0, 30, 60, 90, 120, 150, 180, 210, 235, 240, 245, 255, 265, 270, 275, 300, 330 s and visually inspected.
The video is a construction timelapse with camera zooms and crossfade transitions between scenes.
Workers are visible in every sampled frame; clearest large-person windows were ~30-60 s (concrete pour)
and ~235-270 s (formwork deck).

## Chosen window
- Start: 236 s, Duration: 34 s (236-270 s of source)
- WHY: Static zoomed camera on a formwork deck where 2-4 workers continuously walk across the frame
  carrying materials. Workers are large in frame. Hard-hat variety is excellent for helmet detection:
  a worker with a dark/black hard hat (on phone) dominates 236-250 s; multiple workers with white hard
  hats cross the scene 245-270 s (one carrying plywood sheets across the deck). The camera zooms out at
  ~272 s (frame at 275 s is wide, workers small), so the clip ends at 270 s to avoid the zoom-out.
  The preceding scene transition completes before 235 s, so 236 s starts cleanly inside the static shot.

